    "notes": "### Upgrade notes\n- **Register 0.7.6 on each install.** Use **Build from source** with version `0.7.6` (after `git pull` on Docker and server installs), or upload the release binary. Agents look for an update every hour by default and install it on their own.\n- **There is no Agent 0.7.5.** Some installs built a 0.7.5 from source before this release, and an agent only updates when the version differs, so an official 0.7.5 would never have reached their agents. Agents on a self-built 0.7.5 update to 0.7.6 like any other.\n\n### Changed\n- **The agent empties its test folders before and after every test run.** Test binaries drop files of their own into `C:\\F0` (`/tmp/F0` on Linux and macOS) and into the decoy home folder `fortika-test`, and nothing removed them, so EDR file alerts listed them next to the test that was running. Now the agent empties both before the run starts and again once the result is reported. It also removes every old `task-*` and `cmd-*` run folder before a run. It keeps its own files (`achilles-*`, its config, log and update files) and undo files: any file or folder whose name contains `cleanup`, `restore`, `backup` or `state`, in any case, because some tests leave an undo tool or the saved original state of the host there. After a run it also keeps the test log. If the agent cannot find its own paths, it removes only the test's own binaries. A file that is locked or held by an EDR is skipped and never fails a run. One consequence: a dropped tool or decoy is gone as soon as the run ends, so an EDR scan that runs later, on a schedule or on demand, will not find it. Detections made while the test runs are not affected. System changes a test makes, such as scheduled tasks or firewall rules, are not undone.\n- **Built with Go 1.26.11.** Release binaries were compiled with Go 1.26.0, the minimum that `agent/go.mod` named. The file now carries `toolchain go1.26.11`. To check a download, run `go version -m <binary>`."
